            <ArticleTitle>Unresponsive wheezing to asthma therapy in a 32-year-old female.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>199-202</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Repeat failure of any patient to respond to asthma therapy, particularly corticosteroids, should alert physicians to carry out further pulmonary evaluation. This will prevent unnecessary side effects of asthma therapy and provide prompt treatment for other diseases that may require urgent attention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
